+# Perception vs Control Separation Policy (Architectural Guidance)
+
+Principles:
+- Control loops (servo/actuator) must never be subject to batching-induced latency.
+- Perception pipelines can be batched for throughput but must expose a low-latency "single-sample" channel when needed by control.
+- Use the low-latency service (ops/grpc/low_latency_service.py) for control-critical inference paths.
+- Enforce network and CPU isolation: place control services on isolated CPUs and isolated network namespace where possible.
+- All state-changing commands from perception/planning must pass through a safety filter and verification step before being forwarded to controller (e.g., via ros2_bridge + approvals).
+
+Implementation checklist:
+ - Route control commands to dedicated endpoint and node pool (no batching).
+ - Use RT kernel + CPU isolation for controller processes.
+ - Use PTP for timestamp sync and DDS QoS tuned for deadlines.
+ - Record all actions via evidence SDK for postmortem and certification.
+
